    summary = """# LOWER-FIELD-3 SUMMARY\n\nLF3 moves from endpoint reversal rates to local event anatomy while preserving the LF2 integrity repair and its restrictions.\n\n## Main findings\n\n- A contextual lonely dump is a same-band >=2-sigma downside event with exactly one same-sign >=2-sigma mover in that band/date. Rank-window neighbors are computed with a causal same-date PIT join. Behavioral, correlation, and state neighborhoods remain schema-reserved because no validated fixed peer map is present in LF2. No master isolation score was invented.\n- Isolated 3-sigma downside events are disproportionately temporary shocks: the path map shows stronger 7D reversal/recovery than coordinated events. Deepest isolated cells are thin, so this is a LOCAL_NODE, not a universal rule.\n- Coordinated upside events (`BAND_BROAD_UP`/`MULTI_BAND_UP`) are synchronized and tend toward giveback; continuation/exhaustion divergence is descriptive only.\n- The reversal state machine makes 1-sigma recovery explicit. Recovery, 25/50-percent giveback, full reversal, and new-extreme states are competing event-time observations, not a sequential signal.\n- The LF2 SHMC correction survives: `SHORT_HOT_MEDIUM_HOT` has higher normalized tail probability than SHMC. SHMC-specific activation is dissolved; medium-horizon alignment is a continuation/reversion geometry candidate only.\n- Rank deterioration is retained as a queued rank-health bridge; no death/extinction label is assigned.\n- `BRD_HI + DISP_HI` is the repeated local state with >=50 effective observations and >=3 periods. It raises next-day tail-delivery activity and is consistent with the LF2 breadth gate.\n- The basket implementation is descriptive cohort geometry only. The triangle pilot treats A=Top-500 breadth, B=lower dispersion, C=tail share as one higher-order dependency; no universal mediation claim is made.\n\n## Interpretation\n\nThe lower field changes form with participation: isolated downside shocks are local and rebound-prone, whereas coordinated upside is broad and giveback-prone. This is a participation-topology node, not a trading instruction. Center coupling and tail localization from LF1/LF2 remain intact.\n\n## Limits\n\nMECH-7 was available in the repository but was not consumed by LF3 core generation; the output schema preserves a date-keyed join path so context can be attached later without regenerating core events. Formal behavioral/correlation neighbor maps, 60D censoring, stable trajectory clustering, and execution/tradability audits are not earned. All claims are L0, except breadth-to-delivery as an L1/L2 candidate.\n\n`human_review_required = TRUE`  \n`next_checkpoint_authorized = FALSE`\n"""
    (C.ROOT / "25_LOWER_FIELD_3_SUMMARY.md").write_text(summary, encoding="utf-8")
    decision = """# LOWER-FIELD-3 DECISION\n\n## Verdict\n\n**PASS_LOWER_FIELD_3_LOCAL_EVENT_ANATOMY_WITH_LIMITATIONS**\n\nLF3 earns a local anatomy checkpoint because isolated-down and coordinated-up participation topologies show distinct, reproducible descriptive path shapes, the deep downside reversal remains purge-stable, and the `BRD_HI|DISP_HI` state clears the local-sequence minimum rule.\n\n## Promoted / local / dissolved\n\n- **PROMOTION_CANDIDATE:** `DEEP_DOWNSIDE_REVERSAL`, `DEPTH_TAIL_GRADIENT` (re-scoped from SHMC), and `BREADTH_DISPERSION_DELIVERY`.\n- **LOCAL_NODE:** `ISOLATED_SHOCK_TOPOLOGY`, `COORDINATED_UP_GIVEBACK`, `SHHM_VS_SHMC` continuation/reversion geometry, `LOCAL_BASKET_GEOMETRY`.\n- **DISSOLVE:** SHMC-specific high-tail activation; no master isolation score; any implied death label.\n- **NULL / QUEUED:** residual sector/chain organization remains null; MECH-7 context reuse, full correlation/behavioral neighborhoods, and extinction/decay are queued.\n\n## Answers to final questions\n\n1. Lonely dump = one same-band same-sign >=2-sigma event, with rank-window neighbor residual retained.\n2. All loners in the generated sample are downside by construction; the 3-sigma subset shows recovery/reversal, but thin deepest isolated N limits confidence.\n3. Only two rule-based loner path families clear >=50 events and >=3 quarters; formal unsupervised clustering is not claimed.\n4. Early 1-sigma recovery is the clearest temporary-shock checkpoint in the current anatomy; pre-event discriminators remain L0.\n5. Rank-neighbor context refines isolation materially; other peer families are schema-ready but not validated from LF2.\n6. 1-sigma recovery is a meaningful descriptive stabilization marker, not an executable rule.\n7. Reversal is staged through recovery, giveback, and competing full-reversal/new-extreme paths.\n8. Coordinated-up outcomes tend toward giveback; continuation is not promoted directionally.\n9. Sign x participation topology survives as a local descriptive node, subject to controls in future work.\n10. Rank deterioration is queued as a rank-health bridge, not structural weakness.\n11. SHHM is higher-tail/continuation-like than SHMC; SHMC is reversion-like; this remains descriptive.\n12. High breadth + high dispersion is the asset-level state with the strongest tail-delivery enrichment.\n13. Triangle pilot is associational and limited; it does not establish mediation or synergy.\n14. Subtle-node audit preserves breadth gate, deep reversal, liquidity/rank-health candidates, and dissolves SHMC rescue.\n15. Future tradability audit is required for every candidate; current status is NOT_YET_AUDITED.\n16. Mature enough for future alpha staging: distribution/reversal roles and cross-field/regime roles only, after human review.\n\n`human_review_required = TRUE`  \n`next_checkpoint_authorized = FALSE`  \n`NO STRATEGY · NO PNL · NO EXECUTION`\n"""
    (C.ROOT / "26_LOWER_FIELD_3_DECISION.md").write_text(decision, encoding="utf-8")
